<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST370"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->A Criminal Lawyer<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, June 30, 2004 - 11:13 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Dear BTK, <BR> <BR>Whereas others refuse to listen to your plaintive cries, I&#39;d be happy to listen to your story.  I&#39;m a semiretired criminal lawyer and have represented many killers.  My goal is not to capture or even identify BTK, but to quiet the monster, so that the HURTING STOPS. <BR> <BR>As a criminal defense lawyer, I can find a sympathetic counselor in your area, who will listen to you without snitching.  Rest assured, I will never betray you.  However, I will do everything possible to provide the counseling needed to quiet the monster and STOP THE HURTING. <BR> <BR>To facilitate communication, I&#39;ll reserve an email address for us at your high school &#40;all lower case, minus the word school&#41;@yahoo.com.  Your password will be the nickname of your first camera. <BR> <BR>Take care and I&#39;ll communicate with you soon. <BR> <BR>A Criminal Lawyer <BR>  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 370-->
