<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST886"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->One Big Ho Hum!<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, August 24, 2004 - 11:13 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->So BTK you are 1 big question mark.  And that is not even original.  You seemed to have borrowed that too. Just like all your other messages and deeds.  Experts have mentioned the Zodiac killer and David Berkowitz.  At least David Berkowitz stood up and took resposibility for what he did. <BR>Like Zodiac, you can&#39;t even stand the light of day, because everyone would know you for what you are.  Stand up and take responsibility.  You have already had a criminal lawyer offer you help, shakey as that may be. Unlike MMEad I do not think you are wise.  You are playing a dangerous game.  If you like imitaing, imitate David Berkowitz.  Change your life and make a more postive difference. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 886-->
<!--Post: 893--><!--Time: 1093401845-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST893"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, August 24, 2004 - 7:44 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK: We are waiting. Describe the perfect victim as you perceive her to be. In the ultimate fantasy, tell of the encounter and what that victim has that has drawn you to her. How does she fulfill your dreams of good and evil. <BR> <BR>If I am pleased with your answer, I have a poem for you.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 893-->
<!--Post: 896--><!--Time: 1093421385-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST896"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->A Texan<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, August 25, 2004 - 1:09 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK, <BR>   I admire your ability to avoid being captured. You got in and out of all your victims residences without anyone spotting you well enough to ID you. I just hope that if you are dying you leave some sort of mechanism to enable us to know with absolute certainty who you were. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 896-->
<!--Post: 932--><!--Time: 1093631806-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST932"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Billowy wave<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, August 27, 2004 - 11:36 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If you were drowning I&#39;d swim out to get you.  When I was drowning you only paddled out to see what the fuss was.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 932-->
<!--Post: 938--><!--Time: 1093699852-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST938"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, August 28, 2004 - 6:30 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->And &#34;Wednesday&#39;s child is full of Woe&#34;. BTK, were you born on Wednesday? I was. There are generational curses that come down the family line. They come in all forms, don&#39;t they? It is at times like being unable to get out of the movie theater. We watch in horror and disbelief. Can anyone look in the mirror and then turn away, forgetting his own face? <BR> <BR>Did you kill as a child? I knew a special ed child who attempted his first murder at 2 1/2 years of age. He continued to try to hurt people after that. <BR> <BR>BTK, are you 10 years or so younger than people think that you are? Sophistication usually come with experience and age, but not always. <BR> <BR>ACL, do you know?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 938-->
<!--Post: 948--><!--Time: 1093749832-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST948"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->anon<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, August 28, 2004 - 8:23 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->So how do you get the guy to communicate?  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
