<!--Post: 964--><!--Time: 1094148621-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST964"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->anon<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, September 02, 2004 - 11:10 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I would love to ask a question!  And I include myself in this.  Why are we so obsessed with a nameless, faceless coward who preys on harmless people? This includes fasciantion with the zodiac killer. I ask myself this question daily.  I can understand looking at the patterns of the zodiac killer in regards to btk.  btk seems to have a fascination with using zodiacs methods.  I have not come up with a good reason for following btk.  But I do.  I also notice that there are several of us who are on here regularly.  Any ideas?  Please put forth an explanation that sounds reasonable to me.  I&#39;m just curious.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 964-->
<!--Post: 965--><!--Time: 1094148742-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST965"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:littledaisymae2003@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->anon<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, September 02, 2004 - 11:12 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->btk, do you have any explanations?  Don&#39;t get me wrong, I AM NOT in love with you.  I am curious as to why we are fascinated.  Any answers are thoughtfully considered.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 965-->
<!--Post: 966--><!--Time: 1094154635-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST966"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Screamer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Screamer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, September 02, 2004 - 12:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I became fascinated with serial killers after the Otero&#39;s were murdered behind my grandmothers house. I was 10 years old at the time. I&#39;ve followed BTK and other serial killers ever since. Not really sure why, it is just so far out there in my mind to think that a person could do such crimes. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 966-->
<!--Post: 976--><!--Time: 1094202286-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST976"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nick<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, September 03, 2004 - 2:04 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Because we are human we strive to understand that which detaches many from the very thread of humanity. And with that comes a certain risk, and perhaps responsibilty.   <BR> <BR>&#34;He who fights with monsters might take care lest he thereby become a monster. And if you gaze for long into an abyss, the abyss gazes also into you.&#34; <BR>  <BR>Friedrich Nietzsche <BR>philosopher &#40;1844 - 1900&#41;  <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 976-->
<!--Post: 977--><!--Time: 1094203048-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST977"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->seesthru<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, September 03, 2004 - 2:17 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I remember the message boards about the Baton Rouge Serial killer.  People thought he was monitoring the internet for news and messages about him, and all sorts of stuff.  Turns out he wasn&#39;t online at all.  It is my considered opinion that this BTK isn&#39;t online, and prefers the old method of reading the paper and probably clipping the articles about him.  <BR> <BR>I dont&#39; think he grew with the times, he probalby doesn&#39;t have a DVD player, or a computer.. He lives in the past, stunted, and lonely. He wants fame.   <BR> <BR>Either that, or it&#39;s a clever hoaxter, trying to boost future book sales. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 977-->
<!--Post: 978--><!--Time: 1094203225-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST978"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->seesthru<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, September 03, 2004 - 2:20 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->To BTK, IF you are really out there reading this or any forum... Which I doubt. <BR> <BR>Go ahead and turn yourself in.  You&#39;ll probably not get the death penalty,  because  they will want to interview and study you.  Also,  with appeals you&#39;d die of old age before actually facing the chair or lethal injection, and thst&#39;s even IF  Kansas has the death penalty at all. <BR> <BR>So if you&#39;re fame hungry,  turn yourself in.  They still talk about that Son of Sam, and he was/is a total loser... Just think how much more you could  hear your own voice, see pictures of yourself, andpictures of the faces of all your victims. <BR> <BR>It&#39;s a win/win for you. <BR> <BR> <BR>However I doubt the BTK is even online at all.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 978-->
<!--Post: 987--><!--Time: 1094320346-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST987"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:littledaisymae2003@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->anon<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, September 04, 2004 - 10:52 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK, here&#39;s a poem just for you. <BR>Thriving on someone&#39;s glory is not for you. <BR>Invent yourself over again, <BR>ANd contact us here in.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 987-->
<!--Post: 997--><!--Time: 1094442208-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST997"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->alanbrewers<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, September 05, 2004 - 8:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Kismet is an expression for fate or destiny. <BR> <BR>This is the place to send a message to the tittybaby failure who has labeled himself btk ? <BR> <BR>What a laugh it is to send you a message.You should be renamed tbk. <BR>Too Boring Kismet. <BR> <BR>Everyone knows you read these posts and everyone knows you will not respond.And who cares? <BR>Your destiny/fate has been made obvious by your lack of guts.If there ever was a follow-the-leader-lame-lame-lame-sloppy-ex-juvenil e....It was you.  <BR> <BR>I wasted a few weeks keeping up with this site <BR>and with news of the return of the tbk. <BR>Thanks but no thanks . <BR>I think i will go mow the lawn. <BR> <BR>You always took the cowards way out and that obviously will never change.And if it does i sure wont be around to see it.....Hard to see anything through these bored-to-tears eyes of mine. <BR> <BR>Too Boring Kismet....you are a footnote... <BR>a punchline to a really tired joke. <BR>A waste of everyones time. <BR> <BR>You are such a fool.If you really wanted to be heard you would reach out beyond the local community.Are you the most stupid criminal ever? <BR>There are stupid crook awards now and i see you going over the top. <BR> <BR>Your crimes of the past would be busted within 24 hours these days....You are a bum that was lucky. <BR> <BR>Go crawl back under your rock tbk.  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 997-->
<!--Post: 1003--><!--Time: 1094655741-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1003"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:michaeljames26@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Kyle Brody<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, September 08, 2004 - 8:02 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK,  <BR> <BR>when it comes to the words i would use when referring to you words come to mind such as coward, child, and ignorant. You might think your doing something original here but you&#39;re not. You&#39;re nothing but a Zodiac copycat and you know it. You make the calls to 911 after you kill and write in your pathetic letters because you know and I know that you arent man enough to go after anyone you know you cant handle. Sneaking into homes and killing them in their sleep..who else did that? Let me see...Bundy, Ramirez, The Butcher of New Orleans, Peter Kurten..you get the point you unoriginal bastard? You might be proud of yourself for staying in the dark but heres an example for you. Gary Ridgway...in the 80s they didnt have the technology in forensics to get him but years later they do. The only reason Zodiac hasnt been caught is because all of his methods trace back to the 60s so its much harder but you...mid 70s. How many serials from the 70s got away? None. Berkowitz, Bundy, and even Lucas after the early 80s so its just a matter of time until they get a positive match on your semen and your SALIVA. You didnt think anyone knew about that did you? What did you do? lick the poor girl down? I&#39;ll give you credit for the BTK inituals but thats the only original piece that you have. Face it you pathetic loser, you&#39;re nothing but another copycat. I dont know if you&#39;re responsible for the 6 killings in Kansas as of late but if you were you might as well kiss BTK goodbye. Only a matter of time weakling, and i can promise you i&#39;ll be coming to see you after you are in custody to spit on the face of the most cowardly and weak being that ever lived. Happy hunting you son of a bitch because your time is wearing down. Happy Hunting. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1003-->
<!--Post: 1012--><!--Time: 1094789148-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1012"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->HH Holmes<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, September 09, 2004 - 9:05 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mr. Killman, my personal feeling is that you&#39;re not a resident of Wichita, but live elsewhere in Kansas...or possibly south in Oklahoma City. You&#39;re clearly intelligent, and so you hunted outside the area where you normally live, as other SKs have done over the years. I suspect you&#39;ve even hunted much farther afield, but those are details you&#39;re not yet willing to reveal at this time. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
